  unit: { count: 25, covers: "Counts are what this WU added or rewrote, not the suites they live in (313 core + 27 shell Rust tests and 1015 Vitest tests are green at the tip). Core — src/reach.rs +3: the ordering's rules asserted one at a time (the routed-from address leads, IPv4 outranks IPv6, and IPv6 keeps a stable order below every IPv4 because the flag that would rank it finer is the host's to print and this crate may not ask). Shell — ui/src-tauri/src/setup.rs +3: the hardware-port parser over a real networksetup transcript, a listing that names nothing, and the three hosts that are never asked at all. Front end — setup.test.ts +4: the two probe facts as two, asserted over all eight platforms (this machine's certificate store answers for this machine alone; its system proxy answers for it and for the Simulator), the Simulator's simctl route and its reversal's stated cost, the host guide it now shares, and the absence of the sentence that sent users to a step that cannot work. verdicts.test.ts +4: stepsLeftHere over both probes' full product including the two unknowns it refuses to count, stepsDetail's three wordings and its silence, and the arriving remedy asserted to name no platform. Onboarding.test.tsx +11: the Simulator's three renderings; the collapse rule as an invariant over all eight platforms (a guide is behind a summary exactly where its action is offered) plus a phone's steps read without opening anything; the address offered, disclosed and picked; a refused confirm's note and an allowed confirm's silence; the lead's detail in its four readings — counted, zero-left, probe-unknown, and off-machine. Three existing assertions were re-pointed at the corrected sentences (StatusLine's remedy example, App's arriving remedy, the Simulator's action gate)." }
